                <pb facs="0525" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24595/6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Monroe to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                            Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-18"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 18, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Monroe says Red Cross idea as to providing shelter is excellent, and that
                    there is urgent necessity of houses 24 by 16 feet with siding of ordinary
                    lumber, with light weight, corrugated iron roofs.</p>
            </div>
